sentences.text:
The petitioner is directed to be enlarged on bail in Spl.C.C. No.1652/2023 pending before the Court of Additional City Civil and Sessions Judge, FTS - III, Bengaluru arising out of Crime No.156/2023 registered by Parappana Agrahara Police Station for the offences punishable under Section 9 of the Act and under Sections 4, 5(L), 6 of Sanjay @ Sanju vs The State Of Karnataka By on 19 September, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/60760107/
3 the POCSO Act and under Section 376(2)(n) of IPC, subject to the following conditions:
a) Petitioner shall execute personal bond for a sum of Rs.1,00,000/- (one lakh) with two sureties for the likesum, to the satisfaction of the jurisdictional Court;
b) The petitioner shall appear regularly on all the dates of hearing before the Trial Court unless the Trial Court exempts his appearance for valid reasons;
c) The petitioner shall not directly or indirectly threaten or tamper with the prosecution witnesses;
NC: 2023:KHC:33721 d) The petitioner shall not involve in similar offences in future.
SD/-
